    <DataNode elementId="CPD-18925" textLabel="(+)-nootkatone" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="WTOYNNBCKUYIKC-JMSVASOKSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="350" centerY="310" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="chawkins, SRI, caspi">|FRAME: CPD-21400 (+)-Nootkatone| is a sesquiterpene compound that belongs to the Yashilane series. It was originally characterized as a constltuent of the heartwood essential oil of Alaskan Nootka cypress (|FRAME: TAX-85954|), of which it comprises about 20%. Trace amount was later found in grapefruit (|FRAME: TAX-37656|), where it contributes to the fruit&apos;s distinctive flavor |CITS: [Macleod65]|, and the compound was subsequently found in the peel oils of many other citrus fruits, such as orange, lemon, and mandarin |CITS: [21377882]|. It is now used comprehensively in the pharmaceutical, cosmetic, agricultural and food flavor industries. (+)-Nootkatone is produced from |FRAME: CPD-7989| by the cytochrome P450 enzyme |FRAME: EC-1.14.14.M49|, and is believed to participate in the fruit defense. Many studies were conducted regarding the benefitial effect of |FRAME: CPD-21400| on mammals. It was reported to have extensive benefits including anti-inflammatory response |CITS: [24704449][Chang16][29214688][32392744]|, AMPK activation |CITS: [31280139]|, antibacterial |CITS: [Yamaguchi19][Farha20]|, and anti-insect properties |CITS: [11441443][Guo19][31744055]|. In addition, (+)-nootkatone was found to act as an antitumor compound with antiproliferative, proapoptotic activity and beneficial protective effect |CITS: [29495362][32928152]| that inhibits the anticancer growth of retinoblastoma cells |CITS: [32277665]|. (+)-Nootkatone also possess neuroprotective effects |CITS: [29177693][31422511]| and may be a potential therapeutic treatment for neuroinflammation and Alzheimer&apos;s disease |CITS: [29990697][31542420]|.</Comment>
